/-!
# Finite sign return for the stored rank-four interval packet

The primary argument is a finite quadratic comparison. An exact integer
identity writes the dyadic target as a weighted Gram with nonnegative
pivots. The stored midpoint matrix first pays `25/512` on its diagonal.
After a further diagonal allowance `1/1024`, every absolute comparison
radius row sums to at most `1/1024`; symmetry returns nonnegativity of
the paid midpoint matrix. The stored interval radii have symmetric row
sums at most `25/512`. Therefore any real matrix enclosed entry by entry
by these stored intervals has a nonnegative quadratic form.

All 65 finite rows are checked by deterministic kernel reduction. The
data file fixes the exact endpoint and LDL identities and denominators.
Changing a packed word, sign, pivot or active coordinate is not covered
by these proofs. The exact extraction and the certificate checker share
the same input data and are not independent analytical proofs.

The actual source-entry comparison is OPEN and is the explicit premise
of `paidIntervalSign`. The independent `1/5` high floor at N=64 is OPEN.
No whole-window source paid sign, stage return, cofinal theorem, RH or GRH
is asserted. No equality to the separate 40-bit assembly is asserted.
Independent analytical review: NOT_RUN. Novelty: NOT_ASSESSED.
-/

namespace GRWTSK.NumberTheory.WeilQuadraticForm.RadiusTwoRankFourPaidPacket


